{% doc %}
  Contact — the switchboard.

  Replaces the `sv-page` + Horizon `contact-form` pair on /pages/contact,
  which rendered a serif title over an empty Admin body and then a stock
  form at half width. It was the only page on the site not speaking the
  system, and it was also the only one with no idea what it was for.

  ── What this page is for ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  Three contact surfaces already exist and each owns something:

    /policies/contact-information   the statutory record — registered
                                    address, GSTIN, Grievance Officer.
                                    Furnished by sv-policy.
    /pages/report-a-problem         anything WRONG with an order. It has
                                    a 24-hour clock and needs a video.
    /pages/faq                      the answer, where we already have one.

  What is left for this page is everything that is not a claim: which
  size, is it coming back, where is my parcel, can I collect, and the
  long tail nobody anticipated. And the business it belongs to runs on
  WhatsApp and answers once a working day.

  That is the whole design brief. On a one-reply-a-day promise, a vague
  first message costs a full day — the reply is a question, and the
  answer arrives tomorrow. So this page is not a form with a title on
  it. Its job is to make the first message a good one.

  ── How it is built ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    desk     two columns. You compose on the left, and the message you
             are about to send is written out on the right, in the words
             it will arrive in. Nothing is hidden behind a submit.
    reasons  five. Four compose; the fifth — something arrived wrong —
             does not, and hands off to the claim desk instead. That
             interception is the most important thing on the page: a
             damaged parcel that goes into a contact form loses its
             video and, often, its 24 hours.
    routes   WhatsApp, email, the form. Each carries the same composed
             message, so the channel is a preference and never a
             different conversation.
    desk     the address is an office, not a shop — the one line on this
             page a reader can act on wrongly. The page's single emerald
             moment, as on /policies/contact-information.
    form     in-system rather than Horizon's default, prefilled from the
             draft, and honest about being the slowest way in.
    foot     the statutory record, read from metafields, never typed.

  Every business value — number, email, hours, GSTIN, officer, address —
  comes from Admin. There is no `default:` on any of them: a default is
  a hard-coded business value in disguise and it goes on rendering the
  stale figure after Admin is corrected (ARCHITECTURE.md rule 11).

  Motion contract, per sv-system.css §08: transform and opacity only.
  Every route out is a plain anchor that works with script disabled, the
  form submits without script, and with script off the composer simply
  offers the generic opener rather than a tailored one.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  # Read from Admin, never typed. Two pages that print two different
  # numbers is exactly what a theme setting here would buy us.
  assign wa_raw = shop.metafields.custom.whatsapp_number.value
  assign wa = wa_raw | remove: ' ' | remove: '+' | remove: '-'
  assign mail = shop.metafields.custom.support_email.value
  assign hours = shop.metafields.custom.support_hours.value
  assign officer = shop.metafields.custom.grievance_officer.value
  assign gstin = shop.metafields.custom.gstin.value

  # The number, grouped for reading. Derived from the metafield rather
  # than typed beside it — a second, hand-formatted copy is how the two
  # fall out of step. Any shape we do not recognise is printed whole.
  assign wa_disp = ''
  if wa != blank
    if wa.size == 12
      assign cc = wa | slice: 0, 2
      assign p1 = wa | slice: 2, 5
      assign p2 = wa | slice: 7, 5
      assign wa_disp = '+' | append: cc | append: ' ' | append: p1 | append: ' ' | append: p2
    else
      assign wa_disp = '+' | append: wa
    endif
  endif

  assign addr = shop.address
  assign bg = section.settings.bg_motion
  assign opener = section.settings.prefill_opener
  assign title_a = section.settings.title_a | default: page.title

  # Counted first so a rail can be skipped whole rather than rendering an
  # empty frame around nothing.
  assign n_reason = 0
  assign n_route = 0
  assign n_fact = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    case block.type
      when 'reason'
        assign n_reason = n_reason | plus: 1
      when 'route'
        assign n_route = n_route | plus: 1
      when 'fact'
        assign n_fact = n_fact | plus: 1
    endcase
  endfor
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The registered address, assembled once from the shop's own record
  rather than typed into a block. Guarded on the first line: a shop with
  no address on file would otherwise produce ", , " and render it as a
  fact, which is worse than rendering nothing.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign addr_line = '' -%}
{%- if addr.address1 != blank -%}
  {%- capture addr_line -%}
    {{ addr.address1 }}{% if addr.address2 != blank %}, {{ addr.address2 }}{% endif %}, {{ addr.city }}, {{ addr.province }} {{ addr.zip }}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign addr_line = addr_line | strip -%}
{%- endif -%}

<section class="sv-ct sv-ct--bg-{{ bg }}" data-sv data-sv-contact>

  {%- comment -%}
    Arms the entrance before the section paints — see the snippet's own
    note on why this must be the first child.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'sv-motion-gate' -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    ── The ground ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    The same weave, lights and petals as the FAQ and the claim desk, so
    the three support pages read as one set rather than three designs.
    Decorative only: aria-hidden, no pointer events, carries nothing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless bg == 'off' -%}
    <div class="sv-ct__bg" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="sv-ct__weave"></div>
      <div class="sv-ct__glow sv-ct__glow--a"></div>
      <div class="sv-ct__glow sv-ct__glow--b"></div>
      {%- for i in (1..4) -%}
        <svg class="sv-ct__petal sv-ct__petal--{{ i }}" viewBox="-14 -86 28 92" focusable="false">
          <path d="M0 0 C -9 -30 -6 -62 0 -80 C 6 -62 9 -30 0 0 Z"/>
        </svg>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endunless -%}

  <div class="w sv-ct__inner">

    {%- comment -%} ── Masthead ────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
    <header class="sv-ct__head" data-sv-motion>
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        Line reveal, by line — §08 permits no finer grain. The spans are
        always in the markup; only the motion-ready class turns them
        into a mask, so the title is never left hidden if script fails.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <h1 class="sv-ct__title">
        <span class="sv-ct__line"><span>{{ title_a }}</span></span>
        {%- if section.settings.title_b != blank -%}
          <span class="sv-ct__line"><span>{{ section.settings.title_b }}</span></span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </h1>

      {%- if section.settings.lead != blank -%}
        <p class="sv-ct__lead lead">{{ section.settings.lead }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        ── The desk state ──────────────────────────────────────────
        The hours line is always printed, because it is true whether or
        not script runs. The open / closed pill is not: it is a claim
        about right now, and a claim about right now that is rendered
        server-side is wrong for most of the day it is cached. Script
        fills it against IST and reveals it; with no script the visitor
        simply reads the hours, which is what the page said before.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if hours != blank -%}
        <p class="sv-ct__hours">
          <span class="sv-ct__state" data-sv-state hidden></span>
          <span class="sv-ct__hourstext">{{ hours }}</span>
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    {%- comment -%}
      ── The desk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Two columns, and the split is the argument: what you are building
      on the left, and what it will actually say on the right. The right
      column is sticky, so the message and the way to send it stay
      beside the choice being made rather than waiting at the bottom.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sv-ct__desk">

      {%- comment -%} ── Compose ─────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sv-ct__compose">

        {%- if n_reason > 0 -%}
          <div class="sv-ct__step" data-sv-motion>
            <p class="lab sv-ct__steplab">
              <span class="sv-ct__stepnum">01</span>{{ section.settings.step_reason }}
            </p>

            <ul class="sv-ct__reasons" role="list">
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- if block.type == 'reason' -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    # A reason that names a handoff does not compose a
                    # message at all — it sends the visitor somewhere
                    # this page cannot help them. Everything about the
                    # card changes accordingly, so the distinction is
                    # made once, here.
                    assign is_handoff = false
                    if block.settings.handoff_url != blank
                      assign is_handoff = true
                    endif
                  -%}
                  <li class="sv-ct__reasonwrap" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <button class="sv-ct__reason{% if is_handoff %} sv-ct__reason--away{% endif %}"
                            type="button"
                            aria-pressed="false"
                            data-sv-reason="{{ block.id }}"
                            data-sv-text="{{ block.settings.prefill | escape }}"
                            data-sv-order="{% if block.settings.needs_order %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}"
                            data-sv-away="{% if is_handoff %}1{% else %}0{% endif %}">
                      <span class="sv-ct__reasonart">
                        {%- render 'sv-contact-icon', art: block.settings.art -%}
                      </span>
                      <span class="sv-ct__reasonbody">
                        <span class="sv-ct__reasonlab">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                        {%- if block.settings.note != blank -%}
                          <span class="sv-ct__reasonnote">{{ block.settings.note }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            ── Order number ────────────────────────────────────────
            Hidden until a reason asks for it, because on three of the
            five reasons there is no order yet and an empty field is a
            question the visitor cannot answer. Revealed rather than
            inserted, so nothing is ever created after paint.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="sv-ct__step sv-ct__step--slot" data-sv-orderstep hidden>
            <label class="lab sv-ct__steplab" for="sv-ct-order">
              <span class="sv-ct__stepnum">02</span>{{ section.settings.step_order }}
            </label>
            <input class="sv-ct__field" id="sv-ct-order" type="text"
                   inputmode="text" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
                   placeholder="{{ section.settings.order_placeholder | escape }}"
                   data-sv-orderin>
            {%- if section.settings.order_note != blank -%}
              <p class="sv-ct__fieldnote">{{ section.settings.order_note }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          <div class="sv-ct__step sv-ct__step--slot" data-sv-extrastep hidden>
            <label class="lab sv-ct__steplab" for="sv-ct-extra">
              <span class="sv-ct__stepnum" data-sv-extranum>03</span>{{ section.settings.step_extra }}
            </label>
            <textarea class="sv-ct__field sv-ct__field--area" id="sv-ct-extra"
                      rows="3" data-sv-extrain
                      placeholder="{{ section.settings.extra_placeholder | escape }}"></textarea>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        ── The draft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
        The message, written out in the words it will arrive in. This is
        the page's one real idea: a person who can see their own opening
        line writes a better one, and a better opening line is a day
        saved on a promise of one reply a day.

        The paragraph is a live region so the change is announced rather
        than only drawn, and it holds the generic opener from the
        server, which is exactly what an unscripted visitor sends.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <aside class="sv-ct__side">
        <div class="sv-ct__draft" data-sv-motion>
          <p class="lab sv-ct__draftlab" data-sv-draftlab>{{ section.settings.draft_label }}</p>

          <p class="sv-ct__drafttext" data-sv-draft aria-live="polite">{{ opener }}</p>

          {%- comment -%}
            The handoff. Not a card that appears from nowhere: it is the
            draft's other face, and it replaces the message because when
            this reason is chosen there is no message to send from here.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'reason' and block.settings.handoff_url != blank -%}
              <div class="sv-ct__away" data-sv-awaycard="{{ block.id }}" hidden>
                {%- if block.settings.handoff_label != blank -%}
                  <p class="lab sv-ct__awaylab">{{ block.settings.handoff_label }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if block.settings.handoff_title != blank -%}
                  <p class="sv-ct__awaytitle">{{ block.settings.handoff_title }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if block.settings.handoff_body != blank -%}
                  <p class="sv-ct__awaybody">{{ block.settings.handoff_body }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
                <a class="btn sv-ct__awaygo" href="{{ block.settings.handoff_url }}">
                  {{ block.settings.handoff_cta }}
                </a>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}

          {%- if section.settings.draft_note != blank -%}
            <p class="sv-ct__draftnote" data-sv-draftnote>{{ section.settings.draft_note }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          ── Routes ────────────────────────────────────────────────
          Three ways out, carrying the same message. Every one is a
          plain anchor with the generic opener already in its href, so
          the page works whole before a line of script runs; the script
          only makes the message more specific than it was.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if n_route > 0 -%}
          <div class="sv-ct__routes" data-sv-motion data-sv-routes>
            <p class="lab sv-ct__routelab">{{ section.settings.routes_label }}</p>

            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == 'route' -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign kind = block.settings.kind
                  assign opener_enc = opener | url_encode
                  assign href = block.settings.url
                  assign ext = false

                  case kind
                    when 'whatsapp'
                      assign href = 'https://wa.me/' | append: wa | append: '?text=' | append: opener_enc
                      assign ext = true
                    when 'email'
                      assign subj = section.settings.mail_subject | url_encode
                      assign href = 'mailto:' | append: mail | append: '?subject=' | append: subj | append: '&body=' | append: opener_enc
                  endcase

                  # A route whose channel has no value in Admin is not
                  # rendered at all. A WhatsApp button with no number
                  # behind it is worse than no button.
                  assign usable = true
                  if kind == 'whatsapp' and wa == blank
                    assign usable = false
                  endif
                  if kind == 'email' and mail == blank
                    assign usable = false
                  endif
                  if kind == 'link' and href == blank
                    assign usable = false
                  endif
                -%}

                {%- if usable -%}
                  <a class="sv-ct__route sv-ct__route--{{ kind }}"
                     href="{{ href }}"
                     {% if ext %}target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}
                     {% if kind == 'whatsapp' %}data-sv-wa{% elsif kind == 'email' %}data-sv-mail{% endif %}
                     {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <span class="sv-ct__routeart">
                      {%- render 'sv-contact-icon', art: block.settings.art -%}
                    </span>
                    <span class="sv-ct__routebody">
                      <span class="sv-ct__routetop">
                        <span class="sv-ct__routename">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                        {%- if block.settings.meta != blank -%}
                          <span class="sv-ct__routemeta">{{ block.settings.meta }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </span>
                      {%- if block.settings.note != blank -%}
                        <span class="sv-ct__routenote">{{ block.settings.note }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                    <span class="sv-ct__routego" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                  </a>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}

            {%- if wa_disp != blank -%}
              <p class="sv-ct__plain">
                {{ section.settings.plain_label }}
                <a href="tel:+{{ wa }}">{{ wa_disp }}</a>
                {%- if mail != blank %} · <a href="mailto:{{ mail }}">{{ mail }}</a>{% endif -%}
              </p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </aside>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      ── The form ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Kept, and kept honest. It is the slowest route on the page and the
      copy says so; it exists for the person who will not open another
      app, and for anyone who wants a written record of what they asked.

      Built from Liquid's own contact form tag rather than Horizon's
      block, so the draft can prefill it and the fields can carry the
      order number and the reason as named custom fields. It posts to
      the same inbox either way.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sv-ct__formwrap" id="sv-ct-form" data-sv-motion>
      <div class="sv-ct__formhead">
        <p class="lab">{{ section.settings.form_label }}</p>
        <h2 class="sv-ct__formtitle">{{ section.settings.form_title }}</h2>
        {%- if section.settings.form_note != blank -%}
          <p class="sv-ct__formnote">{{ section.settings.form_note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- form 'contact', class: 'sv-ct__form', id: 'sv-ct-contact-form' -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <p class="sv-ct__sent" role="status" tabindex="-1" data-sv-sent>
            {{ section.settings.form_success }}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if form.errors -%}
          <div class="sv-ct__errors" role="alert">
            {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="sv-ct__grid">
          <p class="sv-ct__f">
            <label class="sv-ct__flab" for="sv-ct-name">{{ section.settings.f_name }}</label>
            <input class="sv-ct__field" id="sv-ct-name" type="text" name="contact[name]"
                   autocomplete="name" value="{{ form.name }}" required>
          </p>

          <p class="sv-ct__f">
            <label class="sv-ct__flab" for="sv-ct-email">{{ section.settings.f_email }}</label>
            <input class="sv-ct__field" id="sv-ct-email" type="email" name="contact[email]"
                   autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" value="{{ form.email }}" required>
          </p>

          <p class="sv-ct__f">
            <label class="sv-ct__flab" for="sv-ct-phone">{{ section.settings.f_phone }}</label>
            <input class="sv-ct__field" id="sv-ct-phone" type="tel" name="contact[phone]"
                   autocomplete="tel" value="{{ form.phone }}">
          </p>

          <p class="sv-ct__f">
            <label class="sv-ct__flab" for="sv-ct-orderno">{{ section.settings.f_order }}</label>
            <input class="sv-ct__field" id="sv-ct-orderno" type="text"
                   name="contact[Order number]" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
                   data-sv-formorder>
          </p>

          <p class="sv-ct__f sv-ct__f--wide">
            <label class="sv-ct__flab" for="sv-ct-body">{{ section.settings.f_body }}</label>
            <textarea class="sv-ct__field sv-ct__field--area" id="sv-ct-body"
                      name="contact[body]" rows="6" required
                      data-sv-formbody>{{ form.body }}</textarea>
          </p>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Named so the reply lands with the reason already attached —
          the same triage the composer made, carried into the inbox.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="contact[Reason]" value="" data-sv-formreason>

        <div class="sv-ct__submit">
          <button class="btn" type="submit">{{ section.settings.form_submit }}</button>
          {%- if section.settings.form_fine != blank -%}
            <span class="sv-ct__fine sv-fine">{{ section.settings.form_fine }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      ── The one clause, stated once ───────────────────────────────────
      The single dark object on the page, and it only works while there
      is exactly one of it — which is why it sits HERE and not up in the
      composer column, where it would have stood shoulder to shoulder
      with the claim-desk handoff and turned the page's one emerald
      moment into two competing ones.

      Here is also where it belongs on the merits. It is a fact about
      the address, so it introduces the address: the switchboard first,
      then the ways in, then the record — and the warning at the top of
      the record, where somebody reading off a postal address is about
      to act on it. It is the one line on a contact page a reader can
      act on wrongly and end up standing outside an office in Anayara
      with nothing to collect.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.rule_title != blank -%}
      <aside class="sv-ct__rule" data-sv-motion>
        <span class="sv-ct__ruleart">{%- render 'sv-contact-icon', art: 'door' -%}</span>
        <div class="sv-ct__rulebody">
          {%- if section.settings.rule_label != blank -%}
            <p class="lab sv-ct__rulelab">{{ section.settings.rule_label }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          <h2 class="sv-ct__ruletitle">{{ section.settings.rule_title }}</h2>
          {%- if section.settings.rule_body != blank -%}
            <div class="sv-ct__rulecopy">{{ section.settings.rule_body }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.rule_link_url != blank and section.settings.rule_link_label != blank -%}
            <a class="sv-ct__rulelink" href="{{ section.settings.rule_link_url }}">
              {{ section.settings.rule_link_label }}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </aside>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      ── The statutory foot ────────────────────────────────────────────
      The record, not the conversation. Each value reads from Admin, and
      a fact with nothing behind it contributes nothing — no label, no
      dash, no placeholder (ARCHITECTURE.md rule 11).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if n_fact > 0 -%}
      <div class="sv-ct__foot" data-sv-motion>
        <dl class="sv-ct__facts">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'fact' -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign val = ''
                case block.settings.source
                  when 'address'
                    assign val = addr_line
                  when 'gstin'
                    assign val = gstin
                  when 'officer'
                    assign val = officer
                  when 'hours'
                    assign val = hours
                  when 'email'
                    assign val = mail
                  when 'whatsapp'
                    assign val = wa_disp
                  else
                    assign val = block.settings.value
                endcase
              -%}
              {%- if val != blank -%}
                <div class="sv-ct__fact" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                  <dt class="lab lab--grey">{{ block.settings.label }}</dt>
                  <dd class="sv-ct__factval">{{ val }}</dd>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </dl>

        {%- if section.settings.foot_link_url != blank and section.settings.foot_link_label != blank -%}
          <a class="act sv-ct__footlink" href="{{ section.settings.foot_link_url }}">
            {{ section.settings.foot_link_label }}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript && document.currentScript.closest('[data-sv-contact]');
      if (!root) return;

      var calm = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

      var WA    = {{ wa | json }};
      var MAIL  = {{ mail | json }};
      var OPEN  = {{ opener | json }};
      var SUBJ  = {{ section.settings.mail_subject | json }};

      /* ── The desk state ───────────────────────────────────────────
         A claim about right now, so it is made in the browser and
         never in a cached page. Computed in IST regardless of where
         the visitor's clock is set — the desk is in Kerala and the
         question is whether anyone is at it. */
      (function () {
        var el = root.querySelector('[data-sv-state]');
        if (!el) return;

        var days  = {{ section.settings.open_days | json }};   /* 1=Mon … 7=Sun */
        var from  = {{ section.settings.open_from | json }};
        var until = {{ section.settings.open_until | json }};
        if (!days) return;

        var now  = new Date();
        var ist  = new Date(now.getTime() + (now.getTimezoneOffset() * 60000) + (5.5 * 3600000));
        var dow  = ist.getUTCDay() || 7;                        /* JS Sunday 0 → 7 */
        var mins = ist.getUTCHours() * 60 + ist.getUTCMinutes();

        var open = days.split(',').indexOf(String(dow)) !== -1 &&
                   mins >= from * 60 && mins < until * 60;

        el.textContent = open
          ? {{ section.settings.state_open | json }}
          : {{ section.settings.state_shut | json }};
        el.className = 'sv-ct__state sv-ct__state--' + (open ? 'open' : 'shut');
        el.hidden = false;
      })();

      /* ── Shared state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
         One object, one writer. The reason, the order number and the
         extra line all funnel through paint(), so the draft, the
         WhatsApp link, the mailto and the form can never disagree
         about what the visitor is asking. */
      var reason = null;   /* { id, text, needsOrder, away } */
      var order  = '';
      var extra  = '';

      var btns      = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-reason]'));
      var waLinks   = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-wa]'));
      var mailLinks = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-mail]'));
      var awayCards = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-awaycard]'));

      var draftEl  = root.querySelector('[data-sv-draft]');
      var draftLab = root.querySelector('[data-sv-draftlab]');
      var noteEl   = root.querySelector('[data-sv-draftnote]');
      var routesEl = root.querySelector('[data-sv-routes]');
      var orderStep = root.querySelector('[data-sv-orderstep]');
      var extraStep = root.querySelector('[data-sv-extrastep]');
      var extraNum  = root.querySelector('[data-sv-extranum]');
      var orderIn   = root.querySelector('[data-sv-orderin]');
      var extraIn   = root.querySelector('[data-sv-extrain]');

      var formBody   = root.querySelector('[data-sv-formbody]');
      var formOrder  = root.querySelector('[data-sv-formorder]');
      var formReason = root.querySelector('[data-sv-formreason]');

      /* The composer is only ever useful with script. Revealing it here
         rather than in the markup means a visitor without script sees
         the routes and the form and nothing that does not work. */
      root.classList.add('sv-ct--live');

      /* An entrance an element never got to play. A block that was
         `hidden` while the observer swept has no box, so it never
         intersects and would come back at opacity 0 for good. When we
         put it back we finish its entrance outright rather than
         animating in something the visitor has already seen. */
      function settle(el) {
        el.classList.add('sv-vis');
        el.classList.add('sv-settled');
      }

      /* ── The message ──────────────────────────────────────────────
         Composed rather than templated, so an empty field drops its
         clause instead of leaving "Order ." hanging. */
      function message() {
        var out = OPEN;
        if (reason && reason.text) out += ' ' + reason.text;
        if (order) out += ' My order number is ' + order + '.';
        if (extra) out += ' ' + extra;
        return out;
      }

      function paint() {
        var away = reason && reason.away;
        var msg  = message();

        /* The draft and the handoff are one slot with two faces. When
           the reason is one this page cannot serve, there is no message
           to show, so the message is not shown — label, text, note and
           the routes under it all step aside together. */
        if (draftEl)  draftEl.hidden  = !!away;
        if (draftLab) draftLab.hidden = !!away;
        if (noteEl)   noteEl.hidden   = !!away;
        if (routesEl) { routesEl.hidden = !!away; if (!away) settle(routesEl); }
        awayCards.forEach(function (card) {
          card.hidden = !(away && card.getAttribute('data-sv-awaycard') === reason.id);
        });

        if (away) return;

        if (draftEl) draftEl.textContent = msg;

        waLinks.forEach(function (a) {
          a.href = 'https://wa.me/' + WA + '?text=' + encodeURIComponent(msg);
        });

        mailLinks.forEach(function (a) {
          var subject = SUBJ + (order ? ' — ' + order : '');
          a.href = 'mailto:' + MAIL +
            '?subject=' + encodeURIComponent(subject) +
            '&body=' + encodeURIComponent(msg);
        });

        /* The form is prefilled, never overwritten. Once somebody has
           typed into it, it is theirs — a composer that keeps clearing
           a half-written paragraph is worse than one that does nothing. */
        if (formBody && !formBody.dataset.svTouched) formBody.value = msg;
        if (formOrder && !formOrder.dataset.svTouched) formOrder.value = order;
        if (formReason) formReason.value = reason ? reason.label : '';
      }

      function applyReason(next) {
        reason = next;

        btns.forEach(function (b) {
          var on = !!next && b.getAttribute('data-sv-reason') === next.id;
          b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', on ? 'true' : 'false');
          b.classList.toggle('is-on', on);
        });

        /* The order field is asked for only where there is an order to
           name, and the numbering closes up behind it rather than
           leaving a gap where step 02 used to be. */
        var wantsOrder = !!next && next.needsOrder && !next.away;
        if (orderStep) orderStep.hidden = !wantsOrder;
        if (!wantsOrder && orderIn) { orderIn.value = ''; order = ''; }

        if (extraStep) extraStep.hidden = !next || next.away;
        if (extraNum)  extraNum.textContent = wantsOrder ? '03' : '02';

        paint();
      }

      btns.forEach(function (b) {
        b.addEventListener('click', function () {
          var id = b.getAttribute('data-sv-reason');

          /* A second click on the chosen reason clears it. Nothing on
             this page should be a one-way door. */
          if (reason && reason.id === id) { applyReason(null); return; }

          applyReason({
            id: id,
            text: b.getAttribute('data-sv-text') || '',
            label: (b.querySelector('.sv-ct__reasonlab') || {}).textContent || '',
            needsOrder: b.getAttribute('data-sv-order') === '1',
            away: b.getAttribute('data-sv-away') === '1'
          });
        });
      });

      if (orderIn) {
        orderIn.addEventListener('input', function () {
          order = orderIn.value.trim();
          paint();
        });
      }

      if (extraIn) {
        extraIn.addEventListener('input', function () {
          extra = extraIn.value.trim().replace(/\s+/g, ' ');
          paint();
        });
      }

      [formBody, formOrder].forEach(function (el) {
        if (!el) return;
        el.addEventListener('input', function () { el.dataset.svTouched = '1'; });
      });

      /* A returning visitor lands on the confirmation, not the top of a
         page they have already read. */
      var sent = root.querySelector('[data-sv-sent]');
      if (sent) sent.focus();

      paint();

      /* ── Reveal on scroll ─────────────────────────────────────────
         Same contract as sv-faq, sv-policy and the claim desk: fires
         once, then unobserves, and a timer pins each entrance to its
         finished state shortly after it should have arrived. Nothing
         here may depend on a transition completing in order to be
         read, and a throttled tab does not advance transitions. */
      if (!calm && 'IntersectionObserver' in window) {
        root.classList.add('sv-motion-ready');

        var held = Array.prototype.slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-motion]'));

        var reveal = function (el) {
          if (el.classList.contains('sv-vis')) return;
          el.classList.add('sv-vis');
          mo.unobserve(el);
          setTimeout(function () { el.classList.add('sv-settled'); }, 1800);
        };

        var mo = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
          entries.forEach(function (en) { if (en.isIntersecting) reveal(en.target); });
        }, { rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px', threshold: 0.06 });

        held.forEach(function (el) { mo.observe(el); });

        /* The masthead is above the fold by definition. Waiting on an
           observer to confirm what is already on screen buys nothing
           but a chance of a blank one. */
        var head = root.querySelector('.sv-ct__head');
        if (head) reveal(head);

        /* An observer reports a state, not every state an element
           passed through. Scroll hard enough in one gesture and a
           block can go from below the fold to above it without a
           callback seeing it intersect, and it would stay invisible
           for good. The sweep closes that.

           On `document` in capture, never on `window`: this theme
           scrolls .page-wrapper, so a window scroll listener never
           fires here. */
        var queued = false;
        var sweep = function () {
          queued = false;
          var fold = window.innerHeight;
          held.forEach(function (el) {
            if (!el.classList.contains('sv-vis') &&
                el.getBoundingClientRect().top < fold) reveal(el);
          });
        };

        document.addEventListener('scroll', function () {
          if (queued) return;
          queued = true;
          setTimeout(sweep, 180);
        }, { capture: true, passive: true });

        setTimeout(sweep, 1200);
      }
    })();
  </script>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Colour, spacing, type scale and motion all come from sv-system.css.
     Nothing below invents a token; where a value looks new it is a
     token with an opacity on it. */

  .sv-ct {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow-x: clip;
    padding: var(--d) 0 var(--f);
  }

  /* Compound, not bare: `.w` sets max-width at (0,1,0) and whichever of
     the two files loads last would otherwise decide the measure. */
  .sv-ct .sv-ct__inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 1080px;
  }

  /* ── The ground ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__bg {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .sv-ct__weave,
  .sv-ct__glow,
  .sv-ct__petal { position: absolute; }

  /* Two crossing thread fields. Each layer translates by exactly one
     tile of its own gradient, which is what makes the loop seamless —
     anything else visibly jumps at the wrap. */
  .sv-ct__weave {
    inset: -40px;
    opacity: 0.44;
    background-image:
      repeating-linear-gradient(64deg, rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.10) 0 1px, transparent 1px 34px),
      repeating-linear-gradient(-64deg, rgba(20, 82, 74, 0.07) 0 1px, transparent 1px 44px);
  }

  .sv-ct__glow {
    width: 62vw;
    height: 62vw;
    max-width: 760px;
    max-height: 760px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    filter: blur(70px);
    opacity: 0.46;
  }

  .sv-ct__glow--a {
    top: -16vw;
    right: -20vw;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.30), transparent 68%);
  }

  .sv-ct__glow--b {
    bottom: 6vw;
    left: -22vw;
    background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(20, 82, 74, 0.16), transparent 70%);
  }

  .sv-ct__petal {
    width: 30px;
    fill: var(--emerald);
    opacity: 0.05;
  }

  .sv-ct__petal--1 { top: 14%; left: 5%;  width: 40px; }
  .sv-ct__petal--2 { top: 41%; right: 7%; width: 26px; }
  .sv-ct__petal--3 { top: 68%; left: 9%;  width: 34px; }
  .sv-ct__petal--4 { top: 88%; right: 5%; width: 44px; }

  .sv-ct--bg-subtle .sv-ct__weave { opacity: 0.22; }
  .sv-ct--bg-subtle .sv-ct__glow  { opacity: 0.28; }
  .sv-ct--bg-subtle .sv-ct__petal { opacity: 0.03; }

  /* Slow enough to read as weather rather than animation. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .sv-ct--bg-full .sv-ct__weave { animation: sv-ct-weave 44s linear infinite; }
    .sv-ct--bg-full .sv-ct__glow--a { animation: sv-ct-drift-a 38s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
    .sv-ct--bg-full .sv-ct__glow--b { animation: sv-ct-drift-b 46s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
    .sv-ct--bg-full .sv-ct__petal { animation: sv-ct-adrift 30s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
    .sv-ct--bg-full .sv-ct__petal--2 { animation-duration: 38s; animation-delay: -6s; }
    .sv-ct--bg-full .sv-ct__petal--3 { animation-duration: 34s; animation-delay: -14s; }
    .sv-ct--bg-full .sv-ct__petal--4 { animation-duration: 42s; animation-delay: -22s; }
  }

  @keyframes sv-ct-weave   { to { transform: translate3d(34px, 44px, 0); } }
  @keyframes sv-ct-drift-a { to { transform: translate3d(-5vw, 6vw, 0) scale(1.1); } }
  @keyframes sv-ct-drift-b { to { transform: translate3d(6vw, -5vw, 0) scale(1.08); } }
  @keyframes sv-ct-adrift  {
    from { transform: translate3d(0, 0, 0) rotate(-8deg); }
    to   { transform: translate3d(14px, -28px, 0) rotate(10deg); }
  }

  /* ── Masthead ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__head { max-width: 40ch; }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__title {
    margin-top: var(--b);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.4rem);
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  .sv-ct__line { display: block; overflow: hidden; }
  .sv-ct__line > span { display: block; }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__lead {
    margin-top: var(--b);
    max-width: 44ch;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  /* The desk state. The pill is the only place on the page where gold
     and emerald sit side by side at small scale, which is what makes it
     read as a signal rather than a label. */
  .sv-ct__hours {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px var(--a);
    margin-top: var(--b);
    padding-top: var(--a);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.32);
  }

  .sv-ct__state {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 5px 14px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .sv-ct__state::before {
    content: '';
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: currentColor;
  }

  .sv-ct__state--open { background: rgba(20, 82, 74, 0.10); color: var(--emerald); }
  .sv-ct__state--shut { background: rgba(124, 119, 109, 0.12); color: var(--grey); }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__hourstext {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  /* ── The desk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* 7:5, not equal columns — the composing is the work and the draft is
     the witness, and equal columns would claim otherwise. */
  .sv-ct__desk {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7fr 5fr;
    gap: var(--d) var(--f);
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: var(--f);
  }

  .sv-ct__side { position: sticky; top: var(--b); }

  /* ── Steps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__step + .sv-ct__step { margin-top: var(--c); }

  .sv-ct__steplab {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: var(--a);
  }

  .sv-ct__stepnum {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    text-transform: none;
    color: var(--tan);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* The composer only does anything with script, so it only appears
     with script. Without it the page is the routes and the form, both
     of which work. */
  .sv-ct__step,
  .sv-ct__reasons { display: none; }

  .sv-ct--live .sv-ct__step { display: block; }
  .sv-ct--live .sv-ct__step[hidden] { display: none; }
  .sv-ct--live .sv-ct__reasons { display: grid; }

  /* ── Reasons ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__reasons {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .sv-ct__reasonwrap { display: block; }

  .sv-ct__reason {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--a);
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    padding: var(--a);
    text-align: left;
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.30);
    border-radius: var(--r-img);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      border-color var(--micro) var(--e),
      box-shadow var(--std) var(--e),
      transform var(--micro) var(--e);
  }

  .sv-ct__reason:hover {
    border-color: var(--tan);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-s);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .sv-ct__reason.is-on {
    border-color: var(--emerald);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-s), inset 0 0 0 1px var(--emerald);
  }

  /* The handoff reason is marked before it is chosen. A person whose
     parcel arrived torn should be able to see, at a glance, that this
     one is not the same kind of thing as the other four. */
  .sv-ct__reason--away { border-style: dashed; }

  .sv-ct__reasonart {
    flex: none;
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .sv-ct__reasonart svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--emerald);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .sv-ct__reasonart .sv-ct-gold { stroke: var(--tan); }

  .sv-ct__reasonbody { display: block; }

  .sv-ct__reasonlab {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-ct__reasonnote {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 5px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  /* ── Fields ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__field {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 13px var(--a);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--card);
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.34);
    border-radius: var(--r-img);
    transition: border-color var(--micro) var(--e), box-shadow var(--micro) var(--e);
  }

  .sv-ct__field::placeholder { color: var(--grey); opacity: 0.66; }

  .sv-ct__field:focus {
    border-color: var(--emerald);
    box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 var(--tan);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .sv-ct__field--area { resize: vertical; line-height: 1.6; }

  .sv-ct__fieldnote {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  /* ── The one clause ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* Sits between the form and the record, and is capped to the record's
     own measure so the two read as one closing block rather than a card
     that happens to be above a list. */
  .sv-ct__rule {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--b);
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-top: var(--f);
    padding: var(--c);
    background: var(--emerald);
    color: var(--cream);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-s);
  }

  .sv-ct__ruleart { flex: none; width: 40px; height: 40px; }

  .sv-ct__ruleart svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    fill: none;
    stroke: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.7);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .sv-ct__ruleart .sv-ct-gold { stroke: var(--tan); fill: var(--tan); }

  /* Compound: `.lab` paints gold at (0,1,0), and gold on emerald fails
     contrast at label scale. */
  .sv-ct .sv-ct__rulelab { color: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.56); }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__ruletitle {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__rulecopy p {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    max-width: 52ch;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.8);
  }

  .sv-ct__rulelink {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--b);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--cream);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--tan);
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    transition: opacity var(--micro);
  }

  .sv-ct__rulelink:hover { opacity: 0.66; }

  /* ── The draft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* Raised above the ground, because it is the one object on the page
     that is about to leave it. */
  .sv-ct__draft {
    padding: var(--b);
    background: var(--card);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-s);
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.26);
  }

  .sv-ct__draftlab { margin-bottom: var(--a); }

  /* Serif, because this is the only copy on the page written in the
     visitor's own voice rather than ours. The gold mark before it is
     the quote opening. */
  [data-sv] .sv-ct__drafttext {
    position: relative;
    max-width: none;
    padding-left: var(--a);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.16rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-ct__drafttext::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 4px;
    bottom: 4px;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--tan);
    border-radius: 1px;
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__draftnote {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    padding-top: var(--a);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--cream-2);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  /* ── The handoff ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__away {
    padding: var(--b);
    margin: calc(var(--b) * -1);
    background: var(--emerald);
    color: var(--cream);
    border-radius: var(--r-card);
  }

  .sv-ct .sv-ct__awaylab { color: var(--tan); }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__awaytitle {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    line-height: 1.24;
    max-width: none;
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__awaybody {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    max-width: none;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.8);
  }

  /* Compound: `.btn` sets background and colour at (0,1,0), and on the
     emerald card the button has to invert. */
  .sv-ct .sv-ct__awaygo {
    margin-top: var(--b);
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  .sv-ct .sv-ct__awaygo:hover { background: var(--card); }

  /* ── Routes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__routes { margin-top: var(--b); }
  .sv-ct__routelab { margin-bottom: var(--a); }

  .sv-ct__route {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--a);
    padding: 14px var(--a);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: var(--r-img);
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    transition:
      background-color var(--micro) var(--e),
      border-color var(--micro) var(--e),
      transform var(--micro) var(--e);
  }

  .sv-ct__route + .sv-ct__route { margin-top: 6px; }

  .sv-ct__route:hover {
    background: var(--card);
    border-color: rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.34);
    transform: translateX(3px);
  }

  /* The primary route is the one the business actually answers on, and
     it is the only one carrying the emerald. */
  .sv-ct__route--whatsapp {
    background: var(--emerald);
    border-color: var(--emerald);
  }

  .sv-ct__route--whatsapp:hover { background: var(--emerald-d); border-color: var(--emerald-d); }
  .sv-ct__route--whatsapp .sv-ct__routename { color: var(--cream); }
  .sv-ct__route--whatsapp .sv-ct__routemeta { color: var(--tan); }
  .sv-ct__route--whatsapp .sv-ct__routenote { color: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.72); }
  .sv-ct__route--whatsapp .sv-ct__routego  { color: var(--cream); }
  .sv-ct__route--whatsapp .sv-ct__routeart svg { stroke: rgba(251, 247, 239, 0.82); }
  .sv-ct__route--whatsapp .sv-ct__routeart .sv-ct-gold { stroke: var(--tan); }

  .sv-ct__routeart { flex: none; width: 26px; height: 26px; }

  .sv-ct__routeart svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--emerald);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .sv-ct__routeart .sv-ct-gold { stroke: var(--tan); }

  .sv-ct__routebody { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }

  .sv-ct__routetop {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px 10px;
  }

  .sv-ct__routename {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-ct__routemeta {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  .sv-ct__routenote {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 3px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  .sv-ct__routego { flex: none; color: var(--tan); font-size: 1rem; }

  /* An email address is one unbreakable token and this line carries two
     of them. Without this it runs off the side of a phone rather than
     wrapping. */
  .sv-ct__plain {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--grey);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .sv-ct__plain a {
    color: var(--emerald);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
    text-decoration-color: var(--tan);
  }

  /* ── The form ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__formwrap {
    margin-top: var(--f);
    padding-top: var(--d);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.32);
  }

  .sv-ct__formhead { max-width: 52ch; }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__formtitle {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__formnote {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  .sv-ct__form { margin-top: var(--c); max-width: 760px; }

  .sv-ct__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--a) var(--b);
  }

  /* Each field wrapper is a <p>, and §02's `[data-sv] p` caps it at 56ch
     from (0,1,1) — which would pinch the inputs inside their columns. */
  [data-sv] .sv-ct__f { margin: 0; max-width: none; }
  .sv-ct__f--wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }

  .sv-ct__flab {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--grey);
  }

  .sv-ct__submit {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--a) var(--b);
    margin-top: var(--b);
  }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__fine { max-width: 42ch; color: var(--grey); }

  [data-sv] .sv-ct__sent {
    max-width: none;
    margin-bottom: var(--b);
    padding: var(--a) var(--b);
    background: rgba(20, 82, 74, 0.08);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--emerald);
    border-radius: var(--r-img);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  .sv-ct__errors {
    margin-bottom: var(--b);
    padding: var(--a) var(--b);
    background: var(--cream-2);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--tan);
    border-radius: var(--r-img);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-ct__errors ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.4em; }

  /* ── The statutory foot ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-ct__foot {
    margin-top: var(--c);
    padding-top: var(--c);
  }

  .sv-ct__facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--b) var(--c);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .sv-ct__fact { margin: 0; }

  .sv-ct__factval {
    margin: 10px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-ct__footlink { display: inline-block; margin-top: var(--c); }

  /* ── Motion ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* Armed by the gate snippet, released by the observer. Transform and
     opacity only, per §08. */
  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion] {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(var(--rise));
    transition: opacity 0.85s var(--entrance), transform 0.85s var(--entrance);
  }

  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
  }

  /* Once settled, the entrance stops owning the element — a throttled
     tab must never leave a block half-transitioned. */
  .sv-ct [data-sv-motion].sv-settled {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
    transition: none;
  }

  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready .sv-ct__line > span {
    transform: translateY(108%);
    transition: transform 0.95s var(--e);
  }

  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready .sv-ct__head.sv-vis .sv-ct__line > span { transform: none; }
  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready .sv-ct__line:nth-child(2) > span { transition-delay: 0.09s; }

  /* The marks draw themselves as their card arrives. stroke-dashoffset
     is neither a layout property nor unbounded — the exception §08
     already allows. */
  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready .sv-ct__reasonart svg :is(path, line, circle, rect, polyline) {
    stroke-dasharray: 260;
    stroke-dashoffset: 260;
    transition: stroke-dashoffset 1.1s var(--e);
  }

  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis .sv-ct__reasonart svg :is(path, line, circle, rect, polyline) {
    stroke-dashoffset: 0;
  }

  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis .sv-ct__reasonwrap:nth-child(2) .sv-ct__reasonart svg * { transition-delay: 0.08s; }
  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis .sv-ct__reasonwrap:nth-child(3) .sv-ct__reasonart svg * { transition-delay: 0.16s; }
  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis .sv-ct__reasonwrap:nth-child(4) .sv-ct__reasonart svg * { transition-delay: 0.24s; }
  .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis .sv-ct__reasonwrap:nth-child(5) .sv-ct__reasonart svg * { transition-delay: 0.32s; }

  .sv-ct [data-sv-motion].sv-settled .sv-ct__reasonart svg * {
    stroke-dasharray: none;
    stroke-dashoffset: 0;
    transition: none;
  }

  /* ── Narrow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .sv-ct__desk {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--c);
      margin-top: var(--d);
    }

    /* Sticky in one column would park the draft over the reasons it is
       meant to be describing. */
    .sv-ct__side { position: static; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .sv-ct { padding: var(--c) 0 var(--d); }

    .sv-ct__reasons { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .sv-ct__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .sv-ct__rule { flex-direction: column; gap: var(--a); padding: var(--b); }
    .sv-ct__formwrap,
    .sv-ct__foot { margin-top: var(--d); }
    .sv-ct__submit .btn { width: 100%; text-align: center; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .sv-ct__weave,
    .sv-ct__glow,
    .sv-ct__petal { animation: none !important; }

    .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion],
    .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready .sv-ct__line > span {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }

    .sv-ct.sv-motion-ready .sv-ct__reasonart svg * {
      stroke-dasharray: none;
      stroke-dashoffset: 0;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV Contact",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "sv-ct-mount",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Masthead" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Talk to us" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title_a",
      "label": "Title, first line",
      "info": "Blank falls back to the page title.",
      "default": "One family,"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title_b", "label": "Title, second line", "default": "one inbox." },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "lead",
      "label": "Lead",
      "default": "The people who packed your parcel are the people who answer. Tell us what it is about and we will write a message worth sending."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The desk state" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The hours line itself comes from the shop metafield custom.support_hours. These settings only decide when the open or closed pill shows, in IST."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "open_days",
      "label": "Open days",
      "info": "Comma separated, 1 = Monday to 7 = Sunday.",
      "default": "1,2,3,4,5,6"
    },
    { "type": "range", "id": "open_from", "label": "Opens (IST hour)", "min": 0, "max": 23, "step": 1, "default": 10 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "open_until", "label": "Closes (IST hour)", "min": 1, "max": 24, "step": 1, "default": 19 },
    { "type": "text", "id": "state_open", "label": "Open label", "default": "At the desk now" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "state_shut", "label": "Closed label", "default": "Away from the desk" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The composer" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "step_reason", "label": "Step 1 label", "default": "What is it about?" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "step_order", "label": "Order number label", "default": "Your order number" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "order_placeholder", "label": "Order number placeholder", "default": "SV-1043" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "order_note",
      "label": "Order number note",
      "default": "On your confirmation email and your packing slip."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "step_extra", "label": "Extra line label", "default": "Anything to add" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "extra_placeholder",
      "label": "Extra line placeholder",
      "default": "Optional — a size, a style name, a date."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "prefill_opener",
      "label": "How every message opens",
      "info": "The first words of the WhatsApp message, the email and the form. Everything the visitor chooses is added to it.",
      "default": "Hi Sahasra Vastra,"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "draft_label", "label": "Draft label", "default": "Your message" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "draft_note",
      "label": "Draft note",
      "default": "We answer once a working day, so the more your first message says, the sooner it is settled."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Routes" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "routes_label", "label": "Routes label", "default": "Send it" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "plain_label", "label": "Plain details label", "default": "Or plainly:" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "mail_subject", "label": "Email subject", "default": "A question for Sahasra Vastra" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The one clause" },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The page's single dark card. It only works while there is exactly one of it — leave the title blank to remove it rather than adding a second."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "rule_label", "label": "Label", "default": "Before you travel" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "rule_title",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "The address is an office, not a shop."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "rule_body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "<p>There is no counter and no rail to browse. Collection is free and genuinely welcome, but by appointment only — message us first, agree a time, and bring your order number. Please do not travel without arranging a slot.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "rule_link_label", "label": "Link label", "default": "Arrange a collection" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "rule_link_url", "label": "Link" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The form" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "form_label", "label": "Label", "default": "The slow way" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "form_title", "label": "Title", "default": "Or write it here" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "form_note",
      "label": "Note",
      "default": "This reaches the same inbox as the email above and is answered in the same working day. Use it if you would rather not open another app — and it fills itself in from whatever you chose above."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "f_name", "label": "Name field", "default": "Your name" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "f_email", "label": "Email field", "default": "Email" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "f_phone", "label": "Phone field", "default": "Phone (optional)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "f_order", "label": "Order field", "default": "Order number (if you have one)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "f_body", "label": "Message field", "default": "Your message" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "form_submit", "label": "Submit label", "default": "Send it" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "form_success",
      "label": "Success message",
      "default": "Thank you — it is with us. We answer within one working day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "form_fine",
      "label": "Fine print",
      "default": "We use what you send only to answer you. See our Privacy Policy."
    },

    { "type": "header", "content": "The statutory foot" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "foot_link_label", "label": "Link label", "default": "Full contact information" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "foot_link_url", "label": "Link" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Ground" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "bg_motion",
      "label": "Background",
      "options": [
        { "value": "full", "label": "Full — weave, lights and petals drift" },
        { "value": "subtle", "label": "Subtle — the same, quieter and still" },
        { "value": "off", "label": "Off — plain ivory" }
      ],
      "default": "full"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "reason",
      "name": "Reason",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "default": "Choosing a size" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "note", "label": "Note", "default": "Send the two measurements and we will tell you the size." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "art",
          "label": "Mark",
          "options": [
            { "value": "size", "label": "Tape measure" },
            { "value": "transit", "label": "Parcel on the road" },
            { "value": "stock", "label": "Hanger" },
            { "value": "wrong", "label": "Opened packet" },
            { "value": "other", "label": "Speech mark" }
          ],
          "default": "other"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "prefill",
          "label": "What this adds to the message",
          "info": "One sentence, written as the visitor. It is appended to the opener.",
          "default": "I need help choosing a size."
        },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "needs_order", "label": "Ask for an order number", "default": false },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "Hand off instead"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Give a link here and this reason stops composing a message. It shows the card below instead — for anything this page cannot settle."
        },
        { "type": "url", "id": "handoff_url", "label": "Hand off to" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "handoff_label", "label": "Card label", "default": "This one has a clock on it" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "handoff_title", "label": "Card title" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "handoff_body", "label": "Card body" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "handoff_cta", "label": "Card button", "default": "Report a problem" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "route",
      "name": "Route",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "kind",
          "label": "Channel",
          "info": "WhatsApp and email read their address from the shop metafields and carry the composed message. A route whose channel is empty in Admin is not rendered.",
          "options": [
            { "value": "whatsapp", "label": "WhatsApp" },
            { "value": "email", "label": "Email" },
            { "value": "link", "label": "Link" }
          ],
          "default": "whatsapp"
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "default": "WhatsApp" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "meta", "label": "Speed", "default": "Usually the same day" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "note", "label": "Note", "default": "The fastest way in. Photos go straight through." },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "art",
          "label": "Mark",
          "options": [
            { "value": "chat", "label": "Two speech marks" },
            { "value": "mail", "label": "Envelope" },
            { "value": "door", "label": "Door" },
            { "value": "clock", "label": "Clock" }
          ],
          "default": "chat"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "url",
          "label": "Link",
          "info": "Used by the Link channel only. Text rather than a link picker so an on-page anchor such as #sv-ct-form is allowed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "fact",
      "name": "Statutory fact",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label", "default": "Registered address" },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "source",
          "label": "Read from",
          "info": "Everything but Typed comes from Admin and is never restated here. A fact with nothing behind it renders nothing at all.",
          "options": [
            { "value": "address", "label": "Shop address" },
            { "value": "gstin", "label": "GSTIN metafield" },
            { "value": "officer", "label": "Grievance Officer metafield" },
            { "value": "hours", "label": "Support hours metafield" },
            { "value": "email", "label": "Support email metafield" },
            { "value": "whatsapp", "label": "WhatsApp number metafield" },
            { "value": "typed", "label": "Typed below" }
          ],
